      "timestamp_raw": "Dec 9, 2011 12:08:43 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Here's some pics of the  S. flava var. rubricorpora near sumatra, liberty Co, FL.  <br/><br/>Pic taken at night, the darkest clone (clone L) is to the right, and sticks out like a sore thumb:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/SarraceniaetcMay2009256.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>Mother clones to the left, seedlings to the right.  Seedlings are generally a lot better in color and growth than the parent plants:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/Sarracenia5_22_10035.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>seedlings in the front, parent plants in the back.  Some of the best pitchers are produced in the spring.  The color can become more intense as the pitcher ages:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/Sarracenia5_17_10161.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/Sarracenia5_22_10003.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>",
      "body_text": "Here's some pics of the  S. flava var. rubricorpora near sumatra, liberty Co, FL.\nPic taken at night, the darkest clone (clone L) is to the right, and sticks out like a sore thumb:\nMother clones to the left, seedlings to the right.  Seedlings are generally a lot better in color and growth than the parent plants:\nseedlings in the front, parent plants in the back.  Some of the best pitchers are produced in the spring.  The color can become more intense as the pitcher ages:",
